    <DataNode elementId="CPD-15742" textLabel="papaverine" type="Metabolite">
      <Xref identifier="XQYZDYMELSJDRZ-UHFFFAOYSA-N" dataSource="InChIKey" />
      <Graphics centerX="1002.8707275390625" centerY="1515.4193115234375" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="3955e7" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="3955e7" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="PMN, hawkins, SRI, caspi">Papaverine is an opium alkaloid found in the opium poppy. It differs in both structure and pharmacological action from the analgesic (morphine-related) opium alkaloids, and is used primarily in the treatment of visceral spasm, vasospasm (especially those involving the heart and the brain), and the treatment of erectile dysfunction.</Comment>
